<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 07-JUL.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 07-JUL.</headline>
<text>
<p>Hurricane Dolores, with 75 mph winds, is centered about 800 miles southwest of the southern tip of Baja California in the eastern Pacific, moving west northwest at 13 mph. It will continue to track out to sea to the west northwest, strengthening slightly during the next 12 hours, then slowly weakening. It does not threaten land, but it is a threat to shipping.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
